      "kind": "lede",
      "html": "<p>A fire risk assessment is a legal duty first. The Regulatory Reform (Fire Safety) Order 2005 puts it on the responsible person. No new app changes that. An app can help you record the walk fully and get the report out sooner.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "takeaways",
      "heading": "The short version",
      "html": "<ul><li>The Fire Safety Order 2005 asks for a fire risk assessment in most non-domestic buildings in England and Wales.</li><li>The responsible person must have a suitable assessment and act on it.</li><li>PAS 79 is a common method. It is not the law.</li><li>Record significant findings and an action plan. Insurers and enforcers ask to see them.</li><li>Photos taken on site make a stronger record than notes written later.</li><li>Software does not make an assessment valid. You do.</li></ul>"
