      "heading": "What the Fire Safety Order says",
      "html": "<p>The Order covers non-domestic buildings in England and Wales. Scotland and Northern Ireland have their own rules.</p><p>The responsible person is usually the employer, owner or occupier. They must find the fire hazards and the people at risk. They must fix or reduce the risk.</p><p>With five or more staff, the significant findings must be written down. The local fire and rescue authority enforces it. This is a summary, not legal advice.</p>"
    },
